{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>His eye was not dim.</b> This is the horn of light of the face that he received from Sinai, from the expression (Numbers 11:7) ״ועינו כעין הבדולח״, (Ezekiel 1:22) ״כעין הקרח הנורא״." "<b>Nor his natural force abated.</b> His moisture. And since it is the way of the old man that dryness overcomes him and moisture departs from him, Scripture testified here concerning Moses that his moisture did not depart from him. And we find the word לחה with an added ה. And observe that when the prophet was born Scripture added a ה, and now at his death it added too, and this is to declare that the Shekhinah cleaved to him even after his death."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:54:40.640332959Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}